@@ -54,6 +54,31 @@ Bindings are fixed at script start: a newly registered tool is callable in the n
 
 While `codemode` is active, `codemode.mode` in [settings](settings.md#tools) decides how the other tools are presented. With `on` (default) declared tools stay declared, and their descriptions say how to call them from scripts. With `only` they are hidden from the model and listed in the `codemode` description instead, so the model calls them through scripts. Tool declarations in the `codemode` description, `describeTool()`, and `ALL_TOOLS` carry the tools' prompt guidelines, since the system prompt rules only cover declared tools.
 
+## Explicit text pages
+
+The default read result remains a text string or image. For programmatic text processing, request
+`format: "page"` and a positive integer `limit`; `offset` is a positive 1-based integer (default 1).
+
+```js
+let offset = 1, lines = 0;
+for (;;) {
+  const page = await tools.read({ path: "large.txt", format: "page", offset, limit: 500 });
+  if (page.type !== "text_page") throw new Error("Expected a text page");
+  lines += page.lines;
+  if (page.eof) break;
+  offset = page.nextOffset;
+}
+text({ lines });
+```
+
+Pages return raw `text`, `offset`, `lines`, `totalLines`, `nextOffset` (null at EOF), `eof`,
+`truncated` and `truncatedBy` ("lines", "bytes" or null). Model-facing notices are not part of raw text.
+The existing 2000-line/50 KiB safety limits remain: explicit pagination alone sets EOF/nextOffset,
+while truncated describes a safety limit cutting the requested range. An empty file counts as one
+empty line, and a trailing newline adds an empty final line; join consecutive raw pages with "\\n"
+to reconstruct stable text. Images and a line too large to fit one page reject explicitly.
+Each read is independent, not a file snapshot; callers must handle files changing between pages.
+
 ## Bounded workflows
 
 Use one script until the next step needs model judgment or user approval. Keep deterministic pagination,
